# Two of a program's files defining one name is an error (spec 1.13), said
# as that even when the two take different numbers of arguments and the
# program calls one of them. (It was reported as the call giving the wrong
# number of arguments to the other, and a large program that included both
# kept the compiler's index-kind analysis from ending, each definition
# replacing the other's result in turn.)
include "include/two_args_name.patlang"
make a function called two_args_name takes a, b returns r
  return a * b
end
print(two_args_name(3, 2))
print("not reached")
